$\blueD{\text{Line }a}$ has points at $(-4,-4)$ and $(6,3)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{3-(-4)}{6-(-4)} \\\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac{7}{10}}
\end{align}$

$\greenD{\text{Line }b}$ has points at $(-7,7)$ and $(2,-5)$.

>$\begin{align} 
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\\\\\
&= \dfrac{-5-7}{2-(-7)} \\\\\\
&= {\dfrac{-12}{9}}\\\\\\
&=\greenD{-\dfrac{4}{3}}
\end{align}$
